From 0f2c68e122f45d20189cf937fb732855804f2db6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: verkur46 <mohamadrezasahami1999@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 01:31:59 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 026/230] Harden the API responses and make matchday pushes
 survive outages
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Transport: gzip the JSON that earns it (server/http/gzip.ts), drop
X-Powered-By, add nosniff and a strict referrer policy, and type the ESPN
fetchers as unknown instead of any.

Push queue: a next_attempt_at column (plus a partial index on unsent rows)
so a Telegram outage no longer burns all five attempts in one drain, and a
deliverability filter so browser guests, password accounts and dev tokens
never enter the queue.

Sync: missed-flip repairs now retry behind a30-minute backoff instead of
every pass, and the boxscore/Understat/ESPN normalisers pick up the shapes
they were missing.

Reads stay unthrottled while writes keep their limit, and a TEMP AUTH PROBE
(off unless AUTH_PROBE=1) prints how each guest/Telegram login resolved.

